<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Take Mombasa to be on longitude <m>40^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m> and Kampala on <m>33^\circ\,\mathrm{E}</m>. When it is <m>0{9}:{30}</m> local time in Mombasa, what is the local time in Kampala? Use the 24-hour clock.</p><p><fillin characters="3" name="ans1"/> : <fillin characters="3" name="ans2"/>   </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>The earth turns eastwards through <m>15^\circ</m> every hour, so the sun reaches places to the east first. One degree of longitude is <m>4</m> minutes of time.</p><p>The difference in longitude is <m>{7}^\circ</m>, so the time difference is <m>{7} \times 4 = {28}</m> minutes. Kampala is west of Mombasa, so its local time is behind: <m>0{9}:{30}</m> <m>-</m> <m>{28}</m> min <m>= 0{9}:0{2}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>9</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>